WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.900
A chart is a picture written in code.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.125
Today we learn the code.

3
00:00:05.375 --> 00:00:14.275
The key to all of it is a booklet called Chart Number One, which explains every symbol and abbreviation, and the exam draws straight from it.

4
00:00:14.525 --> 00:00:18.450
Start with color, because color tells you the most at a glance.

5
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.750
Buff or tan is land.

6
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.575
Green marks areas that cover and uncover with the tide: mud flats and oyster bars that are dry at low water.

7
00:00:28.825 --> 00:00:30.825
Blue is shallower water.

8
00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:33.125
White is deeper water.

9
00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:35.775
That one feels backward, doesn’t it?

10
00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:39.100
On a chart, the blue is where you run aground.

11
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.775
And magenta, that purplish red, is used for lights, aids to navigation, cables, and restricted areas.

12
00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:48.725
Why magenta?

13
00:00:49.725 --> 00:00:53.300
It stands out, even under a red night-light at the helm.

14
00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.150
When you see it, something there matters.
